{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh rose up at night.</b> What is לילה? That there was darkness like night. He and his servants, for there was no house in which there was not a dead one. Rabbi Natan says: were there then no houses in which there were no firstborn? Rather, when a firstborn died to one of them, he would make him an icon and stand it inside his house, and that night it would be crushed and ground down and swept away, and that day was as harsh in their eyes as the day they buried him. And not only that, but the Egyptians bury them in their houses, and the dogs would enter through the cracks and pull the firstborn out from between their teeth and toss them about, and it was harsh in their eyes as the day they buried him."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:24.728609191Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}